    "question": "Does the direction that the reader agents give to an asset-specific news event (favourable or unfavourable) separate the market-relative return of the asset's perpetual contract from 5 minutes after the publication to 4 hours later, on the lead events of 2023 and 2024? Gate: slope of the return on the sign with one intercept per year, standard error clustered by day, t at least 2.0 with a positive slope, and a positive slope in both years. The descriptive tables show how much of the move happens before the publication and in the first minutes.",
